# WHAT IS TRUE TODAY, AND WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT DONE HERE.
#
# Stored blobs in this repository are CRLF — uniformly, not mixed. Verified with
# `git cat-file blob`, which applies no filters (`git show HEAD:<path>` DOES
# filter on this machine and reports the opposite, which is misleading).
#
# The Phase 0A audit recorded "mixed CRLF and LF" and that was wrong. The tooling
# failure behind it was an editor script comparing lines with `=== "}"` while the
# lines ended in "\r" — a bug in the tool, not inconsistency in the repository.
#
# NO GLOBAL `text=auto eol=lf` HERE, on purpose. Declaring it would not change
# anything today (`git add --renormalize .` alters zero blob hashes under this
# machine's core.autocrlf=true), but it would arm a 966-file rewrite for the next
# person who renormalizes on a differently-configured machine — landing in the
# middle of another operator's book work.
#
# Converting the repository to LF is worth doing. It is a standalone, coordinated
# commit made when main is quiet, not a side effect of a cleanup phase.
#
# What IS pinned below is the set where getting it wrong breaks something.

# Binary — never convert, never diff as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico   binary
*.epub  binary
*.traineddata binary

# Windows shell files must keep CRLF or they fail to run.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Diff these as text even though the extension is unusual.
*.tsv   text
